---Represents the result of a single hyperparameter tuning trial from a training job. The TrainingOutput object that is returned on successful completion of a training job with hyperparameter tuning includes a list of HyperparameterOutput objects, one for each successful trial.
---@class gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__HyperparameterOutput
---@field isTrialStoppedEarly? boolean True if the trial is stopped early.
---@field finalMetric? gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1_HyperparameterOutput_HyperparameterMetric The final objective metric seen for this trial.
---@field trialId? string The trial id for these results.
---@field state? gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__HyperparameterOutputStateEnum|string Output only. The detailed state of the trial.
---@field startTime? string Output only. Start time for the trial.
---@field hyperparameters? gcp.ml_v1.StringMap The hyperparameters given to this trial.
---@field builtInAlgorithmOutput? gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__BuiltInAlgorithmOutput Details related to built-in algorithms jobs. Only set for trials of built-in algorithms jobs that have succeeded.
---@field webAccessUris? gcp.ml_v1.StringMap URIs for accessing [interactive shells](https://cloud.google.com/ai-platform/training/docs/monitor-debug-interactive-shell) (one URI for each training node). Only available if this trial is part of a hyperparameter tuning job and the job's training_input.enable_web_access is `true`. The keys are names of each node in the training job; for example, `master-replica-0` for the master node, `worker-replica-0` for the first worker, and `ps-replica-0` for the first parameter server. The values are the URIs for each node's interactive shell.
---@field endTime? string Output only. End time for the trial.
---@field allMetrics? gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1_HyperparameterOutput_HyperparameterMetricList All recorded object metrics for this trial. This field is not currently populated.

---@alias gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__HyperparameterOutputList gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__HyperparameterOutput[]

---@alias gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__HyperparameterOutputStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"QUEUED"|"PREPARING"|"RUNNING"|"SUCCEEDED"|"FAILED"|"CANCELLING"|"CANCELLED"

---Represents a set of hyperparameters to optimize.
---@class gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__HyperparameterSpec
---@field resumePreviousJobId? string Optional. The prior hyperparameter tuning job id that users hope to continue with. The job id will be used to find the corresponding vizier study guid and resume the study.
---@field maxParallelTrials? number Optional. The number of training trials to run concurrently. You can reduce the time it takes to perform hyperparameter tuning by adding trials in parallel. However, each trail only benefits from the information gained in completed trials. That means that a trial does not get access to the results of trials running at the same time, which could reduce the quality of the overall optimization. Each trial will use the same scale tier and machine types. Defaults to one.
---@field params? gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__ParameterSpecList Required. The set of parameters to tune.
---@field hyperparameterMetricTag? string Optional. The TensorFlow summary tag name to use for optimizing trials. For current versions of TensorFlow, this tag name should exactly match what is shown in TensorBoard, including all scopes. For versions of TensorFlow prior to 0.12, this should be only the tag passed to tf.Summary. By default, "training/hptuning/metric" will be used.
---@field maxTrials? number Optional. How many training trials should be attempted to optimize the specified hyperparameters. Defaults to one.
---@field enableTrialEarlyStopping? boolean Optional. Indicates if the hyperparameter tuning job enables auto trial early stopping.
---@field maxFailedTrials? number Optional. The number of failed trials that need to be seen before failing the hyperparameter tuning job. You can specify this field to override the default failing criteria for AI Platform hyperparameter tuning jobs. Defaults to zero, which means the service decides when a hyperparameter job should fail.
---@field goal? gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__HyperparameterSpecGoalEnum|string Required. The type of goal to use for tuning. Available types are `MAXIMIZE` and `MINIMIZE`. Defaults to `MAXIMIZE`.
---@field algorithm? gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__HyperparameterSpecAlgorithmEnum|string Optional. The search algorithm specified for the hyperparameter tuning job. Uses the default AI Platform hyperparameter tuning algorithm if unspecified.

---@alias gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__HyperparameterSpecAlgorithmEnum "ALGORITHM_UNSPECIFIED"|"GRID_SEARCH"|"RANDOM_SEARCH"

---@alias gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__HyperparameterSpecGoalEnum "GOAL_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"MAXIMIZE"|"MINIMIZE"

---Attributes credit by computing the Aumann-Shapley value taking advantage of the model's fully differentiable structure. Refer to this paper for more details: https://arxiv.org/abs/1703.01365
---@class gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__IntegratedGradientsAttribution
---@field numIntegralSteps? number Number of steps for approximating the path integral. A good value to start is 50 and gradually increase until the sum to diff property is met within the desired error range.

---Represents a training or prediction job.
---@class gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__Job
---@field errorMessage? string Output only. The details of a failure or a cancellation.
---@field trainingOutput? gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__TrainingOutput The current training job result.
---@field labels? gcp.ml_v1.StringMap Optional. One or more labels that you can add, to organize your jobs. Each label is a key-value pair, where both the key and the value are arbitrary strings that you supply. For more information, see the documentation on using labels.
---@field predictionOutput? gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__PredictionOutput The current prediction job result.
---@field etag? string `etag` is used for optimistic concurrency control as a way to help prevent simultaneous updates of a job from overwriting each other. It is strongly suggested that systems make use of the `etag` in the read-modify-write cycle to perform job updates in order to avoid race conditions: An `etag` is returned in the response to `GetJob`, and systems are expected to put that etag in the request to `UpdateJob` to ensure that their change will be applied to the same version of the job.
---@field jobPosition? string Output only. It's only effect when the job is in QUEUED state. If it's positive, it indicates the job's position in the job scheduler. It's 0 when the job is already scheduled.
---@field createTime? string Output only. When the job was created.
---@field trainingInput? gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__TrainingInput Input parameters to create a training job.
---@field startTime? string Output only. When the job processing was started.
---@field endTime? string Output only. When the job processing was completed.
---@field jobId? string Required. The user-specified id of the job.
---@field predictionInput? gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__PredictionInput Input parameters to create a prediction job.
---@field state? gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__JobStateEnum Output only. The detailed state of a job.

---@alias gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__JobList gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__Job[]

---@alias gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__JobStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"QUEUED"|"PREPARING"|"RUNNING"|"SUCCEEDED"|"FAILED"|"CANCELLING"|"CANCELLED"

