---@class gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__Location
---@field capabilities? gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__CapabilityList Capabilities available in the location.
---@field name? string

---@alias gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__LocationList gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__Location[]

---Options for manually scaling a model.
---@class gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__ManualScaling
---@field nodes? number The number of nodes to allocate for this model. These nodes are always up, starting from the time the model is deployed, so the cost of operating this model will be proportional to `nodes` * number of hours since last billing cycle plus the cost for each prediction performed.

---A message representing a measurement.
---@class gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__Measurement
---@field metrics? gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1_Measurement_MetricList Provides a list of metrics that act as inputs into the objective function.
---@field elapsedTime? string Output only. Time that the trial has been running at the point of this measurement.
---@field stepCount? string The number of steps a machine learning model has been trained for. Must be non-negative.

---@alias gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__MeasurementList gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__Measurement[]

---MetricSpec contains the specifications to use to calculate the desired nodes count when autoscaling is enabled.
---@class gcp.ml_v1.GoogleCloudMlV1__MetricSpec
---@field target? number Target specifies the target value for the given metric; once real metric deviates from the threshold by a certain percentage, the node count changes.
